SUPPORTED BY THE DEPARTMENT 
OF CULTURAL PROMOTION, 
MINISTRY OF CULTURE

15
00:02:38,840 --> 00:02:41,800
Congratulations to our Mathematics Team.

16
00:02:41,800 --> 00:02:42,680
OUTSTANDING STUDENT 
AWARD CEREMONY
for winning awards at the Academic Olympiad.

17
00:02:42,680 --> 00:02:43,600
BANGKOK PIPAT SCHOOL 2026
for winning awards at the Academic Olympiad.

18
00:02:43,600 --> 00:02:44,640
for winning awards at the Academic Olympiad.

19
00:02:44,920 --> 00:02:45,240
Hey!

20
00:02:47,560 --> 00:02:48,840
Congratulations!

21
00:02:50,560 --> 00:02:51,520
What's wrong with you?

22
00:02:52,640 --> 00:02:54,200
I really admire you.

23
00:02:54,200 --> 00:02:54,960
You did an amazing job.

24
00:02:54,960 --> 00:02:56,800
You must've worked so hard.

25
00:02:57,160 --> 00:02:58,840
Don't forget to get some rest.

26
00:02:59,160 --> 00:03:00,720
You haven't looked too well lately.

27
00:03:00,720 --> 00:03:02,120
I'm worried about you.

28
00:03:02,960 --> 00:03:03,800
You're talking nonsense.

29
00:03:03,800 --> 00:03:07,480
Please give a round of applause 
for Yodsawit Thiticharoen,

30
00:03:07,480 --> 00:03:09,480
better known as Sun.

31
00:03:10,440 --> 00:03:11,320
Thank you, ma'am.

32
00:03:11,760 --> 00:03:14,400
Heavy metal, right?

33
00:03:15,320 --> 00:03:16,400
Another one of our students

34
00:03:16,400 --> 00:03:20,120
submitted a freestanding sculpture 
and won first place

35
00:03:20,120 --> 00:03:21,920
at the Bangkok Young Artist Competition.

36
00:03:21,920 --> 00:03:25,080
Please congratulate Benyuthon Weeranan.

37
00:03:27,360 --> 00:03:28,880
It's only the first day of school.

38
00:03:31,800 --> 00:03:33,560
(At Bangkok Pipat School,)

39
00:03:33,560 --> 00:03:36,120
(we focus on nurturing our students' happiness.)

40
00:03:36,440 --> 00:03:39,240
(Here, students are encouraged to discover 
who they are)

41
00:03:39,240 --> 00:03:41,160
(and pursue what they truly love)

42
00:03:41,160 --> 00:03:43,920
(throughout their years in secondary school.)

43
00:03:44,400 --> 00:03:46,840
(That's why our school isn't overly strict,)

44
00:03:46,840 --> 00:03:49,520
(and we have only four school rules.)

45
00:03:49,920 --> 00:03:52,720
Rule No. 1: Dress appropriately.

46
00:03:53,160 --> 00:03:56,720
Rule No. 2: Stay away from drugs 
and other vices.

47
00:03:56,840 --> 00:04:00,720
Rule No. 3: Be diligent and 
fulfill your responsibilities.

48
00:04:01,160 --> 00:04:02,720
AND RULE NO. 4

49
00:04:02,720 --> 00:04:04,920
Treat everyone like your best friend.

50
00:04:10,600 --> 00:04:11,200
Ouch!

51
00:04:11,200 --> 00:04:11,760
Hey!

52
00:04:13,200 --> 00:04:14,120
Oh, shit!

53
00:04:14,120 --> 00:04:15,760
You ruined my work!

54
00:04:15,760 --> 00:04:16,440
Shit.

55
00:04:16,880 --> 00:04:19,120
I'm sorry. I didn't mean to.

56
00:04:19,120 --> 00:04:20,480
How are you gonna make up for that?

57
00:04:21,760 --> 00:04:23,160
Sorry, sorry.

58
00:04:23,480 --> 00:04:24,600
Are you gonna make it up to me, huh?

59
00:04:24,800 --> 00:04:26,840
Why'd you push me? I already apologized!

60
00:04:26,840 --> 00:04:28,040
Then why'd you push me back?

61
00:04:28,040 --> 00:04:28,680
What the hell is wrong with you?

62
00:04:28,880 --> 00:04:29,440
Come on.

63
00:04:29,440 --> 00:04:30,000
You want this?

64
00:04:30,000 --> 00:04:30,440
Bring it on.

65
00:04:30,440 --> 00:04:31,200
You want a piece of me?

66
00:04:31,200 --> 00:04:32,000
What the hell is wrong with you?

67
00:04:32,000 --> 00:04:32,600
You want this?

68
00:04:33,840 --> 00:04:34,680
Come here, bitch!

69
00:04:34,840 --> 00:04:35,400
Let go of me!

70
00:04:35,920 --> 00:04:36,520
You asshole!

71
00:04:36,680 --> 00:04:37,600
Calm down.

72
00:04:39,520 --> 00:04:42,000
This is how these two show their affection.

73
00:04:43,000 --> 00:04:44,920
It was even worse last year.

74
00:04:44,960 --> 00:04:46,440
There was screaming.

75
00:04:46,440 --> 00:04:48,120
It was like a bomb went off in the auditorium.

76
00:04:48,120 --> 00:04:49,320
Thank you, ma'am.

77
00:04:55,720 --> 00:04:56,880
Oh, shit!

78
00:04:56,880 --> 00:04:58,840
Eww!!

79
00:05:07,920 --> 00:05:09,120
See you later, ma'am!

80
00:05:17,560 --> 00:05:18,800
Damn!

81
00:05:18,800 --> 00:05:21,160
Even the principal is happy that you 
and Sun are graduating.

82
00:05:21,160 --> 00:05:21,960
Of course.

83
00:05:21,960 --> 00:05:23,520
You are the shit.

84
00:05:23,520 --> 00:05:25,280
-Damn right.
-Everyone, take your seats.

85
00:05:35,960 --> 00:05:41,360
I have an announcement for all 
Grade 12 students today.

86
00:05:41,360 --> 00:05:43,800
You don't have any more time to waste.

87
00:05:46,480 --> 00:05:50,600
Here are the forms for you to fill out
and submit to the Guidance Office.

88
00:05:51,560 --> 00:05:52,600
Pass them to your classmates.

89
00:05:52,920 --> 00:05:53,640
Yes, ma'am.

90
00:05:54,440 --> 00:05:58,240
If you still haven't figured out 
what you want to be,

91
00:05:58,720 --> 00:06:01,160
I have to say, that's quite concerning.

92
00:06:02,080 --> 00:06:05,080
At least I can rest easy about one student.

93
00:06:05,720 --> 00:06:07,160
Sun is the perfect example.

94
00:06:07,320 --> 00:06:09,200
He's fully committed to pursuing athletics.

95
00:06:09,720 --> 00:06:12,480
I'm glad you've found the path that's right for you.

96
00:06:14,760 --> 00:06:16,640
Now, fill out the form.

97
00:06:17,520 --> 00:06:20,440
Read it carefully, complete it,
and return it to me.

98
00:06:23,480 --> 00:06:24,680
Hey, pass me one.

99
00:06:30,720 --> 00:06:32,120
Now that you've won the prize,

100
00:06:32,600 --> 00:06:33,880
you should treat me to something.

101
00:06:35,880 --> 00:06:37,840
Should I just treat you with the trophy?

102
00:06:37,880 --> 00:06:38,880
That's all I got.

103
00:06:39,080 --> 00:06:40,240
I didn't get a dime.

104
00:06:42,480 --> 00:06:43,480
Don't look so sad.

105
00:06:43,840 --> 00:06:45,920
Fine, I'll treat you. 

106
00:06:45,960 --> 00:06:46,560
What do you want to eat?

107
00:06:46,600 --> 00:06:48,520
Coconut Matcha Cloudy?

108
00:06:50,040 --> 00:06:51,480
How fancy is that?

109
00:06:51,680 --> 00:06:52,440
Can't you eat something else?

110
00:06:52,520 --> 00:06:53,640
Something they actually sell at school.

111
00:06:56,920 --> 00:06:59,040
I think... you owe me a buffet.

112
00:06:59,240 --> 00:07:00,280
A buffet?

113
00:07:02,120 --> 00:07:02,880
Look up.

114
00:07:04,280 --> 00:07:06,960
YOTSAWIT THITICHAROEN 
NO. 15 RANKED JUNIOR TENNIS PLAYER

115
00:07:09,600 --> 00:07:14,760
BENYU THARNWEERANAN
FIRST PRIZE WINNER, FREESTANDING SCULPTURE
"BANGKOK YOUNG ARTISTS"

116
00:07:15,600 --> 00:07:17,040
Damn.

117
00:07:22,560 --> 00:07:23,120
Ugh.

118
00:07:23,640 --> 00:07:24,920
There's so much space.

119
00:07:25,480 --> 00:07:26,880
Why'd they have to put my picture next to his?

120
00:07:26,880 --> 00:07:27,960
Damn.

121
00:07:29,560 --> 00:07:30,880
Sheesh.

122
00:07:31,400 --> 00:07:33,880
I don't think Sun looks like he did
when he received the trophy in this picture.

123
00:07:37,120 --> 00:07:39,160
I don't really want to come to school, actually.

124
00:07:40,200 --> 00:07:43,800
The only thing that heals me on the first day of school

125
00:07:44,800 --> 00:07:46,520
is your dim sum, Sun.

126
00:07:48,160 --> 00:07:49,600
Oh, please.

127
00:07:49,680 --> 00:07:51,680
You say that about anything that's free, Keaw.

128
00:07:52,280 --> 00:07:54,760
As for me, I can't wait to play tennis 
with you, Sun.

129
00:07:55,160 --> 00:07:57,120
You disappeared for a tournament during 
the school break.

130
00:07:57,480 --> 00:07:58,840
If you want to play with me that badly,

131
00:07:59,600 --> 00:08:01,080
you can catch me this evening.

132
00:08:01,520 --> 00:08:02,160
Zippo!

133
00:08:02,280 --> 00:08:03,800
Oh, I will.

134
00:08:06,040 --> 00:08:07,640
Hey, Sun.

135
00:08:07,840 --> 00:08:09,160
About PREM’S GAME,

136
00:08:09,160 --> 00:08:10,480
are you really not competing?

137
00:08:10,640 --> 00:08:12,240
Coach Kong asked me to check with you.

138
00:08:12,440 --> 00:08:13,040
I don't think so.

139
00:08:13,560 --> 00:08:15,200
I should let the juniors compete 
and build up their records.

140
00:08:15,480 --> 00:08:17,960
Every time I compete, everyone else withdraws.

141
00:08:18,080 --> 00:08:18,840
Besides,

142
00:08:19,520 --> 00:08:20,720
we're in Grade 12, right?

143
00:08:20,840 --> 00:08:23,360
As club captain, you'll get to recruit new members.

144
00:08:24,840 --> 00:08:26,560
You all listen to me.

145
00:08:27,360 --> 00:08:28,760
If they don't have the potential,

146
00:08:29,440 --> 00:08:30,840
they don't get to join my club.

147
00:08:30,920 --> 00:08:32,440
Hmmm!

148
00:08:32,440 --> 00:08:33,840
Damn!

149
00:08:37,320 --> 00:08:37,720
Hey!

150
00:08:39,560 --> 00:08:41,360
Why are they all staring at Sun?

151
00:08:47,640 --> 00:08:49,040
What the hell?

152
00:08:49,240 --> 00:08:51,960
Hey, Sun, check this out.

153
00:08:52,640 --> 00:08:53,160
What?

154
00:08:55,120 --> 00:08:55,680
What is it?

155
00:08:57,480 --> 00:08:58,320
What is it?

156
00:08:58,680 --> 00:08:59,440
What is it, Sun?

157
00:08:59,440 --> 00:09:00,160
Let me see.

158
00:09:03,480 --> 00:09:04,520
Here he comes.

159
00:09:07,560 --> 00:09:10,560
Is the school worried that
he doesn’t look like he did this morning?

160
00:09:11,080 --> 00:09:11,680
You idiot!

161
00:09:12,040 --> 00:09:13,760
Someone obviously drew that on his face.

162
00:09:13,760 --> 00:09:14,720
But who did it?

163
00:09:22,680 --> 00:09:23,800
-Shit!
-Shit!

164
00:09:50,320 --> 00:09:50,720
Hey!

165
00:09:53,480 --> 00:09:54,400
I can’t.

166
00:09:54,560 --> 00:09:55,760
I thought I’d gotten faster.

167
00:09:55,880 --> 00:09:57,320
What were you doing during the school break?

168
00:10:00,040 --> 00:10:01,360
Hey, should we go now?

169
00:10:01,600 --> 00:10:02,720
You’ll still have to run.

170
00:10:02,960 --> 00:10:04,160
Don’t change the subject.

171
00:10:04,480 --> 00:10:05,560
Get up!

172
00:10:06,000 --> 00:10:07,200
There’s one more game, isn’t there?

173
00:10:07,840 --> 00:10:08,720
-Get up.
-Fine.

174
00:10:09,200 --> 00:10:09,640
Go.

175
00:10:12,040 --> 00:10:12,480
Go.

176
00:10:12,760 --> 00:10:13,280
Come on.

177
00:10:13,600 --> 00:10:14,080
Come on!

178
00:10:14,760 --> 00:10:15,480
One more game.

179
00:10:23,920 --> 00:10:24,320
Hey.

180
00:10:24,920 --> 00:10:26,280
Are you gonna finish it today?

181
00:10:29,480 --> 00:10:31,400
Looks like it’ll take a while.

182
00:10:32,640 --> 00:10:33,920
I’m heading out.

183
00:10:36,160 --> 00:10:37,160
Don’t forget to turn off the lights.

184
00:10:38,120 --> 00:10:38,600
See you.

185
00:10:38,880 --> 00:10:39,240
Yeah.

186
00:10:53,960 --> 00:10:55,120
Has he left?

187
00:11:04,800 --> 00:11:06,400
I even let you walk out before me.

188
00:11:07,280 --> 00:11:08,760
You like me that much?

189
00:11:09,080 --> 00:11:10,440
Is that why you were waiting for me?

190
00:11:14,400 --> 00:11:15,160
Are you insane?

191
00:11:21,960 --> 00:11:22,360
Hey!!

192
00:11:23,360 --> 00:11:24,040
Sun!!

193
00:11:25,040 --> 00:11:27,240
Hey, Sun, wait!!

194
00:11:33,520 --> 00:11:34,880
Have fun waiting for the ferry.

195
00:11:36,680 --> 00:11:37,560
Shit!

196
00:11:37,720 --> 00:11:40,720
I hope the BTS you’re riding breaks down
May the A/C die and the power go out.

197
00:11:40,720 --> 00:11:41,800
Sadhu!

198
00:12:07,400 --> 00:12:07,960
Hey, kid!

199
00:12:11,080 --> 00:12:12,240
Need to get across?

200
00:12:12,760 --> 00:12:13,000
Yeah.

201
00:12:13,560 --> 00:12:15,080
The last ferry already left.

202
00:12:15,240 --> 00:12:17,160
Huh? It did?

203
00:12:17,640 --> 00:12:18,760
How am I supposed to get home?

204
00:12:21,000 --> 00:12:21,920
Want me to give you a ride?

205
00:12:22,720 --> 00:12:23,400
Special price.

206
00:12:24,880 --> 00:12:26,360
Guaranteed to get you home.

207
00:13:12,360 --> 00:13:13,000
Ooh!

208
00:13:13,560 --> 00:13:15,160
Ooh, pull over.

209
00:13:15,360 --> 00:13:15,760
Stop, stop.

210
00:13:15,760 --> 00:13:16,520
Pull over.

211
00:13:18,120 --> 00:13:19,640
Right here.

212
00:13:20,480 --> 00:13:21,360
How much?

213
00:13:21,880 --> 00:13:22,400
A hundred baht.

214
00:13:23,560 --> 00:13:25,080
Here, keep the change.

215
00:13:26,360 --> 00:13:28,040
You drive like a maniac.

216
00:13:28,920 --> 00:13:29,600
See ya.

217
00:13:34,240 --> 00:13:36,280
Such a hurry for? 
Trying to cach a buffalo?

218
00:13:37,760 --> 00:13:38,400
Mind your business.

219
00:13:39,480 --> 00:13:42,520
If you walked this fast, 
even a buffalo couldn't keep up

220
00:13:43,840 --> 00:13:44,920
Buffalo my ass.

221
00:13:48,640 --> 00:13:50,640
See you at home.

222
00:13:53,240 --> 00:13:54,000
Good evening, Dad.

223
00:13:54,800 --> 00:13:55,720
You're back?

224
00:13:55,960 --> 00:13:57,280
Follow me, Bay.

225
00:14:04,400 --> 00:14:04,880
Chun!

226
00:14:06,760 --> 00:14:07,400
Chun!

227
00:14:09,480 --> 00:14:10,400
You, go get Chun.

228
00:14:11,320 --> 00:14:11,920
But he said...

229
00:14:11,920 --> 00:14:12,560
Yeah, yeah.

230
00:14:12,560 --> 00:14:13,880
Go get him now!

231
00:14:15,600 --> 00:14:18,280
SAMING PHON FAI
Damn, it's so hard to get hold of the owner!

232
00:14:19,400 --> 00:14:19,760
Right?

233
00:14:20,360 --> 00:14:22,120
What?

234
00:14:22,560 --> 00:14:25,200
Why the hell are you shouting 
in my restaurant?

235
00:14:25,440 --> 00:14:27,400
You're disturbing my customers.

236
00:14:27,520 --> 00:14:30,400
You own a restaurant too.

237
00:14:30,560 --> 00:14:32,600
You should know better.

238
00:14:32,640 --> 00:14:33,440
What kind of behavior is this?

239
00:14:33,440 --> 00:14:34,640
It's obvious who's the real professional.

240
00:14:34,840 --> 00:14:35,600
Ptui!

241
00:14:35,880 --> 00:14:38,880
Don't act all high and mighty, Chun.

242
00:14:38,880 --> 00:14:42,640
What kind of professional steals customers
behind someone's back?

243
00:14:42,840 --> 00:14:43,440
What?

244
00:14:43,600 --> 00:14:44,280
What are you talking about?

245
00:14:44,640 --> 00:14:46,240
Do you have any proof?

246
00:14:46,400 --> 00:14:48,040
You bet I do.

247
00:14:48,160 --> 00:14:49,960
Here's the proof.

248
00:14:50,520 --> 00:14:52,280
SAMING PHON FAI

249
00:14:52,280 --> 00:14:54,000
I went to the event myself.

250
00:14:54,240 --> 00:14:59,000
They always ordered snack boxes from me,
but all of a sudden, they canceled.

251
00:14:59,280 --> 00:15:01,960
So I went to the event to check.

252
00:15:02,040 --> 00:15:02,760
So what?

253
00:15:03,040 --> 00:15:05,880
If the customer wants to switch restaurants,
that's their choice, isn't it?

254
00:15:05,960 --> 00:15:09,080
"That's their choice, isn't it?"

255
00:15:09,160 --> 00:15:10,240
Listen to this.

256
00:15:10,320 --> 00:15:10,680
What?

257
00:15:10,880 --> 00:15:11,840
Whose voice is this?

258
00:15:11,880 --> 00:15:12,360
What?

259
00:15:12,680 --> 00:15:14,960
(How much did MERLION quote you?)

260
00:15:14,960 --> 00:15:16,240
(I'll beat their price.)

261
00:15:16,320 --> 00:15:20,000
(15% lower... No, make it 20%.)

262
00:15:21,760 --> 00:15:24,960
The customer forwarded me
the messages you sent.

263
00:15:25,120 --> 00:15:26,600
Got anything to say?

264
00:15:27,200 --> 00:15:27,920
So what?

265
00:15:28,640 --> 00:15:29,400
What about you?

266
00:15:29,920 --> 00:15:31,240
You're the one who started it.

267
00:15:31,240 --> 00:15:31,960
What did I do?

268
00:15:31,960 --> 00:15:34,520
You left a one-star review on 
my Google Maps page.

269
00:15:34,560 --> 00:15:34,960
What?

270
00:15:34,960 --> 00:15:35,920
You think I wouldn't know?

271
00:15:35,920 --> 00:15:36,720
Well, I do know.

272
00:15:36,800 --> 00:15:38,720
I lost one customer,

273
00:15:38,720 --> 00:15:40,360
so I took one of yours. 
Problem?

274
00:15:40,400 --> 00:15:41,880
I never left that review.

275
00:15:41,920 --> 00:15:43,480
Quit pretending.

276
00:15:43,480 --> 00:15:46,240
Come here! I'll show you.

277
00:15:46,640 --> 00:15:48,160
Come on, hurry up!

278
00:15:49,400 --> 00:15:49,920
Look!

279
00:15:50,360 --> 00:15:50,920
What's this?

280
00:15:50,920 --> 00:15:51,560
Who’s this?
SAMING PHON FAI
THE PLACE IS FILTHY. RATS EVERYWHERE.

281
00:15:51,560 --> 00:15:52,480
(Look!)
SAMING PHON FAI
THE PLACE IS FILTHY. RATS EVERYWHERE.

282
00:15:52,480 --> 00:15:54,480
(Those are actual rats.)

283
00:15:54,960 --> 00:15:58,120
(Right behind Saming Phon Fai.)

284
00:15:58,120 --> 00:15:58,920
Take a good look.

285
00:15:59,680 --> 00:16:01,040
See the reflection in the clip?

286
00:16:01,040 --> 00:16:02,960
(More like Rat Phon Fai.)
SAMING PHON FAI
THE PLACE IS FILTHY. RATS EVERYWHERE.

287
00:16:02,960 --> 00:16:04,000
(Better watch out.)

288
00:16:04,040 --> 00:16:05,960
That's your reflection!

289
00:16:07,280 --> 00:16:08,200
Damn.

290
00:16:08,600 --> 00:16:10,120
Are you seriously that stupid?

291
00:16:10,400 --> 00:16:11,680
I can't believe you.

292
00:16:12,400 --> 00:16:13,160
And look.

293
00:16:13,680 --> 00:16:14,600
Where did you even film this?

294
00:16:14,600 --> 00:16:15,840
Which alley was it?

295
00:16:15,840 --> 00:16:17,960
You filmed somewhere else and 
claimed it was my restaurant.

296
00:16:18,000 --> 00:16:20,680
I could call the police on you.

297
00:16:21,000 --> 00:16:22,400
Hey, Chun!

298
00:16:23,040 --> 00:16:25,360
No need to go that far.

299
00:16:25,440 --> 00:16:26,960
What year is this?

300
00:16:27,960 --> 00:16:30,000
Haven't you ever heard of free speech?

301
00:16:30,040 --> 00:16:30,640
But...

302
00:16:30,720 --> 00:16:33,560
For the sake of your reputation...

303
00:16:33,640 --> 00:16:34,760
Your reputation.

304
00:16:34,960 --> 00:16:38,120
I'll delete the review, okay?

305
00:16:38,120 --> 00:16:38,640
Okay?

306
00:16:39,440 --> 00:16:41,720
I can see it's hurting your business.

307
00:16:42,040 --> 00:16:43,040
You're losing customers.

308
00:16:44,640 --> 00:16:45,400
-Look.
-Just leave.

309
00:16:45,400 --> 00:16:46,400
Listen, Chun.

310
00:16:46,440 --> 00:16:46,880
What?

311
00:16:46,880 --> 00:16:49,680
Let's call it even.

312
00:16:49,960 --> 00:16:53,520
But if you steal my customers again,

313
00:16:53,760 --> 00:16:56,000
you and I are gonna have a problem! 

314
00:16:56,040 --> 00:16:57,480
This is not a threat.

315
00:16:57,680 --> 00:16:58,400
Remember that.

316
00:17:00,720 --> 00:17:01,560
What a dump!

317
00:17:01,560 --> 00:17:02,880
So annoying!

318
00:17:03,240 --> 00:17:04,080
Think you're tough, huh?

319
00:17:04,080 --> 00:17:05,640
Kicking my furniture.

320
00:17:06,360 --> 00:17:06,840
What?

321
00:17:07,720 --> 00:17:08,920
Come say that at my place!

322
00:17:09,040 --> 00:17:09,840
Get lost!

323
00:17:09,840 --> 00:17:10,960
Damn!

324
00:17:16,120 --> 00:17:17,600
How was your first day at school?

325
00:17:18,440 --> 00:17:19,320
It was fine, Dad.

326
00:17:19,760 --> 00:17:20,400
Nothing much.

327
00:17:21,200 --> 00:17:21,800
Look.

328
00:17:22,560 --> 00:17:25,320
Remember that national team coach
who came to watch you compete?

329
00:17:26,440 --> 00:17:28,840
He said he saw your potential.

330
00:17:29,520 --> 00:17:30,640
And now,

331
00:17:30,840 --> 00:17:33,440
there's one opening at the national 
training camp.

332
00:17:33,480 --> 00:17:35,120
I've already arranged it.

333
00:17:38,720 --> 00:17:39,600
When is it?

334
00:17:40,360 --> 00:17:41,240
October.

335
00:17:42,760 --> 00:17:45,560
So get ready to say goodbye
to your friends.

336
00:17:52,120 --> 00:17:52,760
Yes, Dad.

337
00:17:57,920 --> 00:17:59,000
You won't tell me where you bought it.

338
00:17:59,000 --> 00:17:59,800
I just bought it.

339
00:17:59,800 --> 00:18:01,720
-I bought it.
-Here you go.

340
00:18:01,760 --> 00:18:02,200
I thought you made it yourself.

341
00:18:02,200 --> 00:18:03,000
It's stir-fried noodles.

342
00:18:03,400 --> 00:18:04,560
But I’m not a noodle.

343
00:18:04,600 --> 00:18:05,720
Yeah.

344
00:18:05,720 --> 00:18:06,520
Well, I’ll just dig in.

345
00:18:06,560 --> 00:18:07,080
You're such a noodle.

346
00:18:07,080 --> 00:18:07,680
Touché.

347
00:18:09,160 --> 00:18:10,200
Give me your plate.

348
00:18:10,280 --> 00:18:10,920
Thanks.

349
00:18:11,520 --> 00:18:12,000
Bay.

350
00:18:12,320 --> 00:18:12,760
Yes, Dad?

351
00:18:12,760 --> 00:18:15,840
Have you decided which university 
you're applying to?

352
00:18:16,240 --> 00:18:17,440
I've been looking, Dad.

353
00:18:17,480 --> 00:18:18,160
Hmm.

354
00:18:18,440 --> 00:18:21,640
The university we talked about has already
opened its portfolio applications.

355
00:18:21,800 --> 00:18:23,000
You have so many achievements.

356
00:18:23,000 --> 00:18:25,080
I'm sure you'll get in.

357
00:18:25,320 --> 00:18:28,360
I'm still not sure I want to study there.

358
00:18:28,400 --> 00:18:28,760
Huh?

359
00:18:28,760 --> 00:18:29,840
Just apply first.

360
00:18:29,840 --> 00:18:30,640
Right.

361
00:18:30,720 --> 00:18:31,960
-It won't hurt.
-Right.

362
00:18:31,960 --> 00:18:33,360
If you get accepted, 
we'll talk about it then.

363
00:18:37,120 --> 00:18:37,640
Dad.

364
00:18:37,840 --> 00:18:38,160
Hmm?

365
00:18:39,160 --> 00:18:39,760
Honestly,

366
00:18:39,960 --> 00:18:41,360
do you want me to get into a top university

367
00:18:41,520 --> 00:18:43,360
just so you can brag to the son of that family?

368
00:18:45,360 --> 00:18:46,000
What are you talking about?

369
00:18:48,920 --> 00:18:49,640
I blocked him.

370
00:18:49,640 --> 00:18:50,560
I blocked his dad too.

371
00:18:50,560 --> 00:18:51,720
I don't know anything about them.

372
00:18:51,760 --> 00:18:56,840
You say that, but yesterday I saw you 
using your secret account

373
00:18:56,840 --> 00:19:00,000
to leave troll comments on their son's post
about making the national team.

374
00:19:01,960 --> 00:19:03,160
How the hell did you know that?

375
00:19:03,640 --> 00:19:05,640
I was lurking with my secret account too.

376
00:19:05,720 --> 00:19:08,000
You're becoming more and more 
like your mom.

377
00:19:08,080 --> 00:19:08,640
This boy.

378
00:19:10,840 --> 00:19:11,440
Thanks.

379
00:19:13,360 --> 00:19:14,880
Anyway, think it over.

380
00:19:14,880 --> 00:19:15,720
About college.

381
00:19:16,160 --> 00:19:19,600
It's always good to have a backup plan.

382
00:19:20,280 --> 00:19:22,280
You can study whatever you want.

383
00:19:22,800 --> 00:19:24,480
I just don't want you to become 
another troubled kid.

384
00:19:34,160 --> 00:19:36,480
I only want you to think about it.

385
00:19:36,720 --> 00:19:37,920
That's all.

386
00:19:41,880 --> 00:19:45,320
There's still time for you to decide
to go back to college, Boat.

387
00:19:45,840 --> 00:19:46,360
Honey.

388
00:19:48,040 --> 00:19:48,480
Yeah?

389
00:19:50,560 --> 00:19:51,120
Pass me the kai palo.

390
00:19:59,600 --> 00:20:01,840
FURONG

391
00:20:03,320 --> 00:20:03,720
Here.

392
00:20:04,480 --> 00:20:05,040
Thanks.

393
00:20:13,680 --> 00:20:15,200
Why do you look so happy?

394
00:20:15,880 --> 00:20:17,600
I'm still not used to it.

395
00:20:23,480 --> 00:20:24,760
Anyway, about today,

396
00:20:24,880 --> 00:20:28,160
don't stress over Dad telling you 
to go back to school.

397
00:20:28,440 --> 00:20:29,920
Yeah, I'm used to it.

398
00:20:30,280 --> 00:20:34,400
I'd rather wrap wontons all day
than go back to studying medicine.

399
00:20:35,480 --> 00:20:39,520
But I envy you.
Should I tell Dad you're my role model?

400
00:20:39,520 --> 00:20:40,480
You'd better not.

401
00:20:40,680 --> 00:20:42,040
Like I'm not suffering enough.

402
00:20:42,040 --> 00:20:43,320
Don't you mention me.

403
00:20:48,240 --> 00:20:48,960
What about you?

404
00:20:49,720 --> 00:20:51,680
Why don't you tell dad you want to study abroad?

405
00:20:51,920 --> 00:20:53,400
I've seen you looking up 
tons of information about it.

406
00:20:56,640 --> 00:20:58,480
I know that if I tell him now,

407
00:20:58,800 --> 00:21:01,120
there's no way he'll let me go.

408
00:21:01,680 --> 00:21:05,680
I'll wait until the right time
before I tell him.

409
00:21:07,200 --> 00:21:10,400
And when is "the right time"?

410
00:21:11,440 --> 00:21:12,320
I don't know.

411
00:21:13,480 --> 00:21:15,000
But I know I can do it.

412
00:21:15,840 --> 00:21:16,760
I think...

413
00:21:17,120 --> 00:21:18,480
If I can do it,

414
00:21:19,480 --> 00:21:20,840
then I can do it.

415
00:21:21,400 --> 00:21:22,840
"I can do it! I can do it!"

416
00:21:22,880 --> 00:21:24,320
Just like Dad always says.

417
00:21:25,000 --> 00:21:25,680
"I can do it."

418
00:21:25,680 --> 00:21:26,440
Yeah.

419
00:21:26,440 --> 00:21:27,480
Manifestation?

420
00:21:27,480 --> 00:21:29,280
Of course!

421
00:21:30,000 --> 00:21:31,640
You're becoming more and more like him.

422
00:21:32,760 --> 00:21:33,320
That's a good thing.

423
00:21:36,480 --> 00:21:37,640
Why'd you come all the way out here today?

424
00:21:39,160 --> 00:21:40,560
Well, Dad told me to.

425
00:21:40,960 --> 00:21:42,720
I was taking a walk near the house the other day.

426
00:21:43,080 --> 00:21:47,200
One of the neighbors saw me
and told Dad she'd seen me.

427
00:21:48,480 --> 00:21:49,160
Damn it.

428
00:21:49,520 --> 00:21:50,040
Right.

429
00:21:50,600 --> 00:21:52,160
But Dad really shouldn't be telling people

430
00:21:52,240 --> 00:21:53,880
you're a medical intern at the hospital.

431
00:21:55,440 --> 00:21:55,960
Whatever.

432
00:21:56,440 --> 00:21:58,080
At least we get to explore new routes

433
00:21:58,680 --> 00:22:00,680
so I don't have to worry about anyone 
recognizing me.

434
00:22:01,800 --> 00:22:02,600
If you're okay with that.

435
00:22:10,920 --> 00:22:11,440
Boat!!

436
00:22:14,000 --> 00:22:14,440
Hey!

437
00:22:14,960 --> 00:22:15,800
It's really you!

438
00:22:16,600 --> 00:22:17,080
Hi.

439
00:22:17,320 --> 00:22:18,040
What's up, Bay?

440
00:22:18,120 --> 00:22:19,520
I spoke too soon.

441
00:22:20,680 --> 00:22:21,640
Where the hell have you been?

442
00:22:23,000 --> 00:22:23,280
Umm.

443
00:22:23,320 --> 00:22:23,960
How've you been?

444
00:22:24,360 --> 00:22:25,320
I haven't seen you in...

445
00:22:25,440 --> 00:22:26,160
Hold on, let me...

446
00:22:26,320 --> 00:22:27,000
I freaking miss you!

447
00:22:29,440 --> 00:22:30,120
Hmm.

448
00:22:30,440 --> 00:22:33,080
Does the hospital make you work out?

449
00:22:33,160 --> 00:22:34,280
Or have you been hitting the gym?

450
00:22:34,440 --> 00:22:35,080
You're freaking ripped.

451
00:22:37,120 --> 00:22:37,560
I...

452
00:22:39,560 --> 00:22:40,480
I carry a lot of textbooks.

453
00:22:40,680 --> 00:22:41,440
Textbooks?

454
00:22:41,960 --> 00:22:42,960
They still use those?

455
00:22:42,960 --> 00:22:44,280
They don't use tablets?

456
00:22:44,280 --> 00:22:45,960
I thought they did.

457
00:22:45,960 --> 00:22:47,560
Anyway, which program did you choose?

458
00:22:47,760 --> 00:22:49,000
I wanted to ask you for some advice.

459
00:22:49,000 --> 00:22:50,360
Hey, I should get back to studying.

460
00:22:50,360 --> 00:22:50,840
See you later.

461
00:22:52,120 --> 00:22:52,880
Bay, come on!

462
00:22:53,440 --> 00:22:54,280
Let's go, Bay!

463
00:22:54,440 --> 00:22:55,440
Yeah, yeah.

464
00:22:56,080 --> 00:22:57,120
See you later, Coach.

465
00:22:57,240 --> 00:22:57,720
Hmm.

466
00:23:21,880 --> 00:23:23,680
You do both sculpture and painting. 

467
00:23:24,720 --> 00:23:26,000
Which one do you actually like?

468
00:23:26,440 --> 00:23:27,600
That's none of your business.

469
00:23:28,920 --> 00:23:30,680
I'm not making art at your house.

470
00:23:32,120 --> 00:23:35,680
I'm just wondering
what you really want to do.

471
00:23:36,560 --> 00:23:37,800
Or are you just doing them, 

472
00:23:39,680 --> 00:23:40,720
and when you get bored,

473
00:23:42,880 --> 00:23:44,360
you'll give up again?

474
00:23:44,880 --> 00:23:46,200
Isn't that how it's supposed to be?

475
00:23:47,480 --> 00:23:47,960
And you?

476
00:23:49,080 --> 00:23:50,840
You don't even know what the hell you like.

477
00:23:51,080 --> 00:23:55,400
If your dad hadn't made you play tennis,

478
00:23:56,400 --> 00:23:58,600
would you even know what the hell you like?

479
00:24:12,480 --> 00:24:13,800
I really like tennis.

480
00:24:16,400 --> 00:24:16,960
Yeah.

481
00:24:17,480 --> 00:24:18,320
Good for you.

482
00:24:27,080 --> 00:24:27,800
Damn it.

483
00:24:42,600 --> 00:24:43,520
PREMS'S GAME 31

484
00:24:43,520 --> 00:24:44,560
TENNIS TEAM SELECTION 
MEN'S SINGLES

485
00:24:44,560 --> 00:24:45,480
5:00 P.M. AT THE TENNIS CLUB 
BANGKOK PIPAT SCHOOL

486
00:24:49,440 --> 00:24:49,920
Hey.

487
00:24:50,480 --> 00:24:51,920
They're accepting entries for 
men's singles this year?

488
00:24:52,400 --> 00:24:54,720
Uh, Sun isn't entering this year.

489
00:24:54,880 --> 00:24:56,360
He wants to give the juniors a chance.

490
00:24:57,360 --> 00:24:58,600
Oh.

491
00:24:59,800 --> 00:25:00,960
Are you interested?

492
00:25:01,800 --> 00:25:02,320
Oh, no.

493
00:25:02,680 --> 00:25:03,360
Just asking.

494
00:25:08,600 --> 00:25:09,960
Well, well, well.

495
00:25:09,960 --> 00:25:11,200
How've you been, everyone?

496
00:25:11,520 --> 00:25:12,840
It's been a long school break.

497
00:25:12,840 --> 00:25:14,200
I hope everyone's doing well.

498
00:25:15,080 --> 00:25:15,880
Yes.

499
00:25:15,880 --> 00:25:16,800
Today,

500
00:25:17,000 --> 00:25:20,880
I'd like everyone to loosen up a little.

501
00:25:20,960 --> 00:25:21,680
Does that sound great?

502
00:25:22,000 --> 00:25:23,240
Yes!

503
00:25:23,520 --> 00:25:24,080
Ready?

504
00:25:24,160 --> 00:25:25,280
Ready!

505
00:25:25,720 --> 00:25:28,760
Today's activity is...

506
00:25:28,760 --> 00:25:30,400
Dodgeball!!

507
00:25:38,360 --> 00:25:40,120
How is this supposed to build teamwork?

508
00:25:40,240 --> 00:25:40,840
Ready?

509
00:25:43,960 --> 00:25:44,360
Ready?

510
00:25:45,360 --> 00:25:45,800
Yes!

511
00:25:47,200 --> 00:25:48,160
If you're ready,

512
00:25:51,160 --> 00:25:52,040
begin!!

513
00:26:03,720 --> 00:26:05,280
You'll never hit me!

514
00:26:21,280 --> 00:26:21,960
Oww!

515
00:26:28,280 --> 00:26:28,640
Shit!

516
00:26:45,120 --> 00:26:45,560
Enough!

517
00:26:46,680 --> 00:26:47,320
If you're tired,

518
00:26:47,800 --> 00:26:49,080
just stop.

519
00:26:49,080 --> 00:26:49,880
You stop.

520
00:26:50,000 --> 00:26:51,000
You're not even an athlete.

521
00:26:51,240 --> 00:26:51,840
Just quit.

522
00:27:37,400 --> 00:27:38,080
Shit!

523
00:27:41,200 --> 00:27:42,320
Screw you!

524
00:27:42,440 --> 00:27:42,920
Oww!

525
00:27:43,360 --> 00:27:43,920
Oww!

526
00:27:44,080 --> 00:27:45,080
Are you guys okay?

527
00:27:49,680 --> 00:27:50,000
Shit.

528
00:27:50,000 --> 00:27:50,520
What happened?

529
00:27:57,040 --> 00:27:57,320
Blood!

530
00:27:58,400 --> 00:27:58,880
You're bleeding!

531
00:27:59,600 --> 00:27:59,840
Huh!

532
00:28:01,000 --> 00:28:01,680
Oh, shit!

533
00:28:03,640 --> 00:28:04,040
Hey!

534
00:28:04,920 --> 00:28:05,760
Oh, shit!

535
00:28:05,760 --> 00:28:06,160
Blood!

536
00:28:07,560 --> 00:28:08,800
What the hell did you do?

537
00:28:09,080 --> 00:28:10,080
What the hell did you do?

538
00:28:15,960 --> 00:28:16,320
Wait.

539
00:28:17,720 --> 00:28:18,640
I said wait.

540
00:28:23,560 --> 00:28:24,560
What the hell is it?

541
00:28:25,520 --> 00:28:26,240
What's up, buddy?

542
00:28:30,920 --> 00:28:32,160
I want to ask you something.

543
00:28:32,480 --> 00:28:33,240
Hmm.

544
00:28:37,400 --> 00:28:38,200
This semester,

545
00:28:41,000 --> 00:28:42,400
I want us to call a truce.

546
00:28:44,480 --> 00:28:45,680
Are you messing with me?

547
00:28:48,880 --> 00:28:50,080
Is this some kind of prank show?

548
00:28:50,480 --> 00:28:51,400
I'm serious.

549
00:28:53,840 --> 00:28:55,840
Because this is my last semester.

550
00:29:01,400 --> 00:29:02,320
Your last semester?

551
00:29:03,320 --> 00:29:03,800
Yeah.

552
00:29:04,600 --> 00:29:05,720
I won't be here next semester.

553
00:29:06,240 --> 00:29:07,720
I'll be joining the national team's 
training camp.

554
00:29:10,360 --> 00:29:11,000
What the hell?

555
00:29:12,080 --> 00:29:13,480
You're just gonna leave?

556
00:29:15,640 --> 00:29:16,440
Here's the deal.

557
00:29:18,440 --> 00:29:20,360
You do your thing, and I'll do mine 
this semester.

558
00:29:21,880 --> 00:29:23,040
Next semester,

559
00:29:24,120 --> 00:29:26,640
you'll finally get to live without me 
bothering you.

560
00:29:36,200 --> 00:29:37,120
Deal?

561
00:29:51,200 --> 00:29:52,000
Hey, Sun!

562
00:29:54,280 --> 00:29:55,400
The principal's looking for you.

563
00:29:58,200 --> 00:29:58,520
Okay.

564
00:30:19,320 --> 00:30:21,800
Your father already called me 
about your withdrawal.

565
00:30:21,800 --> 00:30:23,240
PIRUNPORN CHUEAKAEWMANEE
SCHOOL PRINCIPAL

566
00:30:23,240 --> 00:30:25,880
But I didn't want to approve it
until I've spoken with you.

567
00:30:28,720 --> 00:30:29,800
Couldn't you...

568
00:30:30,480 --> 00:30:35,440
keep studying while continuing your training,
like you've been doing?

569
00:30:38,720 --> 00:30:41,720
Joining the training camp gives me
a better chance of making the national team.

570
00:30:41,760 --> 00:30:42,760
So you've already made up your mind,

571
00:30:43,080 --> 00:30:45,320
that this is the path you want to 
dedicate yourself to,

572
00:30:46,080 --> 00:30:47,600
that you truly love tennis?

573
00:30:49,720 --> 00:30:50,360
Yes, ma'am.

574
00:30:50,800 --> 00:30:52,080
Is there anything else

575
00:30:52,080 --> 00:30:53,720
that you love or are interested in?

576
00:30:59,920 --> 00:31:03,400
I'd still like to see you graduate 
alongside your friends.

577
00:31:06,760 --> 00:31:09,000
Honestly,
I'll miss that too.

578
00:31:10,240 --> 00:31:12,120
But now that this opportunity has come my way,

579
00:31:13,360 --> 00:31:14,760
I have to seize it.

580
00:31:15,480 --> 00:31:17,240
Then all I can do is wish you the best,

581
00:31:18,160 --> 00:31:19,680
and hope that this opportunity

582
00:31:19,680 --> 00:31:21,520
is truly what you want.

583
00:31:21,880 --> 00:31:22,960
Thank you, ma'am.

584
00:31:24,760 --> 00:31:25,960
Congratulations, Sun.

585
00:31:27,600 --> 00:31:27,960
Hey!

586
00:31:30,160 --> 00:31:30,880
What are you doing here?

587
00:31:31,360 --> 00:31:32,760
He wanted to see if you're really quitting.

588
00:31:32,760 --> 00:31:33,640
Hey!

589
00:31:35,760 --> 00:31:36,920
He's lying.

590
00:31:37,240 --> 00:31:37,720
Huh?

591
00:31:37,840 --> 00:31:39,080
That's what you said.

592
00:31:40,200 --> 00:31:41,520
If you don't believe me,

593
00:31:41,960 --> 00:31:43,560
you can ask the principal yourself.

594
00:31:44,640 --> 00:31:45,960
But once you get your answer,

595
00:31:47,040 --> 00:31:49,800
I hope you'll keep your word
and really call a truce.

596
00:31:52,040 --> 00:31:54,000
I think he's really leaving.

597
00:31:55,880 --> 00:31:57,240
Hey! Wait!

598
00:32:00,680 --> 00:32:01,880
It's just one semester.

599
00:32:02,520 --> 00:32:03,880
Can't you finish it first before going off to

600
00:32:04,440 --> 00:32:06,440
your national training camp or whatever?

601
00:32:07,680 --> 00:32:11,320
The national team tryouts have their own schedule.

602
00:32:12,760 --> 00:32:13,920
No one's gonna wait for me.

603
00:32:17,320 --> 00:32:18,360
What the hell?

604
00:32:20,800 --> 00:32:21,200
Damn it.

605
00:32:22,600 --> 00:32:23,560
That's so stupid.

606
00:32:26,880 --> 00:32:28,120
What's his problem?

607
00:32:43,760 --> 00:32:45,160
YOTSAWIT THITICHAROEN 
NO. 15 RANKED JUNIOR TENNIS PLAYER

608
00:32:45,160 --> 00:32:46,760
BENYU THARNWEERANAN
FIRST PRIZE WINNER, FREESTANDING SCULPTURE
"BANGKOK YOUNG ARTISTS"

609
00:33:16,440 --> 00:33:17,880
(I won't be here next semester.)

610
00:33:18,200 --> 00:33:19,880
(I'll be joining the national team's 
training camp.)

611
00:33:53,480 --> 00:33:56,600
STORIES WITH THIS TEMPLATE 
ADD YOURS

612
00:34:21,280 --> 00:34:23,800
Is there anything else
that you love or are interested in?

613
00:35:30,360 --> 00:35:32,000
Is he really leaving?

614
00:35:55,520 --> 00:35:57,120
Hello.
ATHLETE REGISTRATION DAY

615
00:35:57,960 --> 00:35:59,240
Welcome, everyone.

616
00:36:11,720 --> 00:36:13,600
Ally, have many people signed up?

617
00:36:14,320 --> 00:36:15,640
Quite a few.

618
00:36:15,760 --> 00:36:16,760
Since you're not competing,

619
00:36:16,760 --> 00:36:18,400
six people have already signed up.

620
00:36:18,920 --> 00:36:19,680
Sun.

621
00:36:20,400 --> 00:36:21,560
Do you really have to go?

622
00:36:21,680 --> 00:36:22,920
Are we never going to play tennis 
together again?

623
00:36:23,040 --> 00:36:23,800
Oh, please.

624
00:36:24,240 --> 00:36:25,960
He's still with us for this whole 
semester, isn't he?

625
00:36:26,000 --> 00:36:26,800
Don't be so dramatic.

626
00:36:27,280 --> 00:36:28,080
By the way,

627
00:36:28,080 --> 00:36:29,640
if you don't make the national team,

628
00:36:29,960 --> 00:36:31,360
I'll be waiting to laugh at you.

629
00:36:31,360 --> 00:36:34,520
Hey! Can't you be a little more sensitive?

630
00:36:34,760 --> 00:36:35,560
Nope, I can't.

631
00:36:38,320 --> 00:36:38,960
How are things going?

632
00:36:39,080 --> 00:36:39,680
Well...

633
00:36:40,480 --> 00:36:42,280
should we close registration now?

634
00:36:42,320 --> 00:36:45,880
Time's almost up,
and I don't think anyone else is coming.

635
00:36:46,920 --> 00:36:47,960
I think so.

636
00:36:48,800 --> 00:36:51,040
Why don't we choose the playing styles
and get started?

637
00:36:52,120 --> 00:36:52,400
Come on.

638
00:36:52,400 --> 00:36:53,360
Wait, Coach!

639
00:37:08,040 --> 00:37:09,200
Hey! What the hell are you doing?

640
00:37:10,240 --> 00:37:10,600
Eh?

641
00:37:11,200 --> 00:37:12,320
I'm signing up.

642
00:37:13,000 --> 00:37:13,880
What else does it look like?

643
00:37:15,800 --> 00:37:16,240
Hey!

644
00:37:16,880 --> 00:37:17,520
What now?

645
00:37:18,160 --> 00:37:19,400
I thought we called a truce. 

646
00:37:19,880 --> 00:37:21,000
A truce?

647
00:37:23,840 --> 00:37:25,280
When did I ever agree to that?

648
00:37:26,080 --> 00:37:27,000
I don't remember.

649
00:37:28,000 --> 00:37:29,480
I never accepted.

650
00:37:29,800 --> 00:37:30,920
Did you get the wrong idea?

651
00:37:51,800 --> 00:37:52,560
Sun.

652
00:37:52,560 --> 00:37:53,200
Damn it, Bay.

653
00:37:53,200 --> 00:37:54,000
TENNIS CLUB

654
00:37:54,000 --> 00:37:54,400
Bay!
TENNIS CLUB

655
00:38:01,920 --> 00:38:03,440
You wanna try me?

656
00:38:05,200 --> 00:38:05,760
Fine.

657
00:38:07,920 --> 00:38:09,560
If you're not calling a truce today,

658
00:38:10,000 --> 00:38:12,000
don't come asking for one later.

659
00:38:13,720 --> 00:38:16,600
Well, I hope this tennis club

660
00:38:17,320 --> 00:38:18,800
has something good for me to try.

661
00:38:27,360 --> 00:38:28,360
Here I am.

662
00:38:37,680 --> 00:38:40,000
TENNIS CLUB

663
00:39:17,200 --> 00:39:19,520
How did he make this shape?

664
00:39:26,040 --> 00:39:26,920
This part is…

665
00:39:28,400 --> 00:39:29,320
How do I fix it?

666
00:39:36,200 --> 00:39:36,720
Ahem!

667
00:39:37,760 --> 00:39:38,480
What are you doing? 

668
00:39:41,960 --> 00:39:42,440
What?

669
00:39:42,440 --> 00:39:43,400
I was just looking.

670
00:39:45,160 --> 00:39:46,200
I didn’t do anything.

671
00:39:50,240 --> 00:39:52,560
Did you feel bad
and wanted to fix it?

672
00:39:54,320 --> 00:39:55,000
You wish.

673
00:39:55,840 --> 00:39:59,520
I saw it was ruined
and I wanted to play with it.

674
00:40:01,800 --> 00:40:03,280
Hmm.

675
00:40:03,800 --> 00:40:04,520
Really?

676
00:40:07,320 --> 00:40:08,600
Doesn’t seem so hard to make.

677
00:40:10,040 --> 00:40:11,120
I don’t know how you won the prize.

678
00:40:20,920 --> 00:40:22,200
- You used to play tennis?

679
00:40:22,200 --> 00:40:22,960
- I did.

680
00:40:23,280 --> 00:40:24,720
- How good were you?

681
00:40:24,720 --> 00:40:25,960
- Are you gonna wipe the floor with Sun?

682
00:40:26,160 --> 00:40:27,280
- You're comparing me to him?

683
00:40:27,360 --> 00:40:28,480
- He's making the national team.

684
00:40:28,880 --> 00:40:30,280
- Then why'd you sign up?

685
00:40:31,960 --> 00:40:33,520
- He won't even be here next semester.|

686
00:40:33,840 --> 00:40:35,640
- Can't you just let him be happy for a little while?

687
00:40:40,000 --> 00:40:41,360
- Why do you hate him so much?

688
00:40:48,200 --> 00:40:48,880
- Honestly…

689
00:40:50,000 --> 00:40:51,400
- I…

690
00:40:53,680 --> 00:40:55,280
- don't really hate him. 

691
00:40:57,200 --> 00:41:00,400
SUPPORTED BY THE DEPARTMENT 
OF CULTURAL PROMOTION, 
MINISTRY OF CULTURE
